   "store_energy_above_mains_kWh",
   "recoverable_energy_above_45C_kWh",
   "minutes_since_last_draw"
  ],
  "observation_notes": "The tank is stratified: delivery temperature is the TOP node, the collector inlet is the BOTTOM node. recoverable_energy_above_45C_kWh is the WP1 E_rec,45 quantity (in Uttarakhand the threshold is the 50 C delivery target; the field keeps its cross-state name) and needs an estimator (not a raw sensor). Loop flow sets stratification, not collector heat, in this model.",
  "safety_shield": {
   "force_bypass_if": "T_water_top_C >= 72.0 (3.0 C guard band below the 75.0 C hard limit, to allow for sensor and control lag)",
   "force_bypass_if_pcm": "T_pcm_C >= 62.0 (PCM-bearing designs only)",
   "clamp_flow_to": "[0.01, 0.05] kg/s",
   "pump_off_below_irradiance_Wm2": 10.0,
   "dry_run": "pump commanded on, flow sensor reads ~0 -> stop pump, raise fault",
   "sensor_failure": "missing reading for a required field -> fall back to bypass (safe default), raise fault",
   "rationale": "Hard requirement carried from the earlier contract. In the current model the shield acts on the TOP water node (start of sub-step) and on the PCM; plain-tank peaks reached 73.3 C in the multi-node model, below the 75 C limit (docs/PROGRESS.md section 6).",
   "note_v2": "Finding: the existing PCM-side shield only blocks CHARGING at 62 C and is not enough for PCMs already above their melt band; some designs exceed 65 C. A design is infeasible if its PCM peak exceeds 65 C in any simulated year."
  }
 },
